 class="paper">
<svg/>
<h1>Comments in a worksheet</h1>
<aside class="note"><span class="note-mark" aria-hidden="true">✎</span><div class="note-body">
<p>A one-line comment is a note for the reader. It supports <em>emphasis</em>, <strong>bold</strong> and maths such as <svg/>, which is typeset but never evaluated.</p>
</div></aside>
<p>A car covers <svg/> in <svg/>, so its speed is</p>
<div class="eq"><svg/></div>
<div class="eq"><svg/></div>
<aside class="note"><span class="note-mark" aria-hidden="true">✎</span><div class="note-body">
<p>The answer is in km/h if <svg/> is in km and <svg/> in hours: a note can sit right after a maths line.</p>
</div></aside>
<aside class="note"><span class="note-mark" aria-hidden="true">✎</span><div class="note-body">
<p>A longer note can run over several lines and hold a list:</p>
<ul>
<li>check the units first</li>
<li>then compare with <svg/></li>
</ul>
<p>Nothing inside, such as <svg/> or the equation below, ever takes effect.</p>
<div class="eq"><svg/></div>
</div></aside>
<p>Doubling the time halves the speed:</p>
<aside class="note off"><span class="note-mark" aria-hidden="true">✎</span><div class="note-body">
<div class="eq"><svg/></div>
<div class="eq"><svg/></div>
</div></aside>
<div class="eq"><svg/></div>
<aside class="note"><span class="note-mark" aria-hidden="true">✎</span><div class="note-body">
<p>Several comment lines in a row
  are one note.</p>
</div></aside>
</main>
</body>
</html>
